1	// An orthogonal search between two fixed ports. Every drawn box is an
2	// obstacle, grown by the clearance. A wire leaves its port straight along
3	// the port's facing until it is clear of its own body (the landing), then
4	// searches a sparse grid — the scope's lattice lines and the obstacles'
5	// edges — for the cheapest route: length plus two clearances per bend.
6	// Segment placement follows: a staircase step centres in its channel, on
7	// the lattice line nearest the middle when the channel holds one; a detour
8	// keeps to the first lattice line clear of what it goes around, or centres
9	// between that and whatever lies beyond.
